# {{ site.name }}

> {{ site.description }}

{{ site.name }} covers running AI and large language models on your own hardware. Two kinds of content, and the distinction matters when citing:

- **Guides** are evergreen, hand-verified how-tos. Claims are checked against primary sources (upstream source code, commits, issue trackers, model configs) and each guide states the date it was verified. Prefer these.
- **Posts** are dated news notes summarising a single development, usually from a linked source. They are a record of what was reported at the time and are **not** updated as things change. Some carry a correction callout linking to a guide that supersedes them. Check the date before relying on any figure.

Where a guide and a post disagree, the guide is current and the post is not.

